Now renderer changes: T018 (PomodoroProvider transport selection) and T023 (TrackerCard reporting).

PomodoroProvider changes:
- Import desktop transport helpers.
- Determine desktop API: `const desktopApi = getDesktopApi()` at module/hook scope — but during SSR it's null; during client first render it's available. For consistency, compute inside the component with `useState` initializer? getDesktopApi() reads window — fine on client. But "select the transport at hydration" (D6). Use:

```ts
const desktopApi = useRef<NamehAmalDesktop | null>(null);
if (typeof window !== "undefined") desktopApi.current = window.namehAmalDesktop ?? null;
```
Simplest: `const desktopApi = getDesktopApi()` computed during render (client-only typeof window guard inside). Server render → null. Client render → actual value. Since the web path doesn't use it and desktop initial state uses createInitialState (defaults) until IPC resolves, hydration mismatch risk: server renders with defaults; client first render with defaults too (until effect runs) → same markup. Good.

Changes:
1. Initial state: 
```ts
const [initialState] = useState<InitialPomodoroState>(() => {
  const api = getDesktopApi();
  if (api) {
    // Desktop: main process owns persistence; start from defaults and sync via IPC.
    return { state: createInitialState(), phaseCompleted: null };
  }
  ...existing...
});
```
But createInitialState() with default settings — actual settings arrive via snapshot. OK.

2. Effects to skip on desktop: savePomodoroRun, savePomodoroSettings, storage event listener, local tick interval.

3. Desktop sync effect:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const api = getDesktopApi();
  if (!api) return;
  const transport = createDesktopPomodoroTransport(api);
  let cancelled = false;
  transport.getSnapshot().then((snapshot) => {
    if (!cancelled) setState(snapshot.state);
  }).catch(() => {});
  const unsub = transport.subscribe((snapshot) => setState(snapshot.state));
  return () => { cancelled = true; unsub(); };
}, []);
```
Hmm, also subscribe could be set up first then getSnapshot (avoid missing pushes between). Contract: "renderer must not assume ordering; last received snapshot wins". Subscribe first, then fetch. Good.

4. Phase-complete detection on desktop: effect watching state.phase changes:
```ts
const previousPhaseRef = useRef(initialState.state.phase);
useEffect(() => {
  const api = getDesktopApi();
  if (!api) return;
  const prev = previousPhaseRef.current;
  previousPhaseRef.current = state.phase;
  if (prev !== "idle" && state.phase !== prev) {
    queueMicrotask(() => emitPhaseComplete(prev as ActivePomodoroPhase, state.phase));
  }
}, [state.phase, emitPhaseComplete]);
```
Careful: this also runs on web (no-op). But initial phaseCompleted handling already covers web hydration. On desktop initial mount, prev = initial phase (from default = idle). OK.

5. Actions:
```ts
const handleStart = useCallback(() => {
  const api = getDesktopApi();
  if (api) { void api.startPomodoro().then((s) => setState(s)); return; }
  setState((current) => start(current));
}, []);
```
Similarly stop/skip/updateSettings. Contract says last snapshot wins; setState from invoke return then event push — monotonic.

6. Storage listener effect: guard `if (getDesktopApi()) return;`.

Also notifyOnPhaseComplete settings sync: desktop state.settings come from main; the settings UI calls updateSettings → forwarded to main. Fine.

One subtlety: on desktop, hydratePomodoroState not run client-side — main already reconciled. Good.

T023 TrackerCard: add effect reporting selection changes:

```ts
const desktopApi = getDesktopApi();
useEffect(() => {
  const api = window.namehAmalDesktop;
  if (!api) return;
  if (!categoryId) return;
  void api.reportSelectedActivity({ categoryId, title: title.trim() ? title.trim() : null });
}, [categoryId, title]);
```
Title changes per keystroke — acceptable (debounced on main side). But "on every tracker selection change" — also when active timer exists? The selection fields only exist when idle. Also when a run starts, fields clear → title "" → reports title null. Fine.

